.TH QWSEC 1 "November 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwsec \- security audit, vulnerability discovery, and exploit analysis using local Qwen3-4B
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qwsec
[\fB\-c\fR \fI16\fR|\fI32\fR|\fI48\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fI0..4\fR]
[\fB\-\-web\fR]
\fItarget\fR
[\fIprompt\fR...]
.PP
.I command
|
.B qwsec
[\fB\-c\fR \fI16\fR|\fI32\fR|\fI48\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fI0..4\fR]
[\fB\-\-web\fR]
[\fIprompt\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwsec
is a specialized security audit tool that inspects source code, decompiled binaries, configs, or piped standard input for vulnerabilities, logic bugs, cryptographic weaknesses, and injection points.
.PP
The model operates under an uncensored security audit profile, analyzing code for OWASP Top 10, CWE categories, memory safety violations (use-after-free, buffer overflows, race conditions), and improper authentication mechanisms without safety refusals.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " tokens"
Set context window size (16, 32, or 48 thousand tokens). Default is 32.
.TP
.BI \-r " level"
Set reasoning effort level (\fI0\fR to \fI4\fR). Default is 2. Higher levels (3 or 4) are recommended for deep vulnerability discovery.
.TP
.B \-\-web\fR, \fB\-\-search
Query Tor SOCKS5h anonymously for live CVE advisories and vulnerability reports affecting detected package dependencies.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Perform air-gapped security audits using the local CVE knowledge base with zero outbound network calls.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Audit a C source file for memory safety and race conditions:
.RS
.nf
qwsec src/driver.c "Identify buffer overflows, format string bugs, and logic flaws"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Audit piped configuration through stdin:
.RS
.nf
sudo cat /etc/ssh/sshd_config | qwsec "Audit SSH daemon security posture"
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .qwignore
Project-level exclusion file to omit sensitive directories, private files, and proprietary packages from security scans and Tor research.
.TP
.I ~/.config/qw/ignore
Global user exclusion rules applied across all repositories.
